FFTW is supplied without modification for non-commercial use.
See www.fftw.org for terms of use and documentation.

This README file has been added to the standard FFTW directory package by Joe Mandeville.
To make the FFTW library for use with "jip" tools, follow these instructions.

Determine the OS and the machine type from unix/Linux:
unix% uname -s
Linux
unix% uname -m
i686

MAKE A DIRECTORY FOR THIS OS/MACHINE IF ONE DOES NOT EXIST: "OS-machine"
unix% mkdir Linux-i686

THEN

From the directory of this README.jbm file:

make distclean
./configure --prefix=$JIP_HOME/fftw-3.2.2/Linux-i686  (where JIP_HOME is the root directory for jip tools)
make install
